#-  §5╔═--═ஓ๑🏭๑ஓ═--═╗§r
        §8A Heist At§r
        SoulCorp!
 §5╚═--═ஓ๑🏭๑ஓ═--═╝§r

§8The §0SoulCorp §8Factory loomed on the other side of the river like a metal beast, the giant chimneys exhaling eerie black smoke with a tint of blue. The factory hummed faintly. 
#- §8So close to the place Sweetpea called home, her beloved tavern. The sound of that factory was like white noise but now it was a constant reminder of the secrets and power inside. She hated betraying the trust of §0Enocori§8, one of her friends who shared in the same ‘spooky’ lifestyle.§r
#- §8But she knew even he had secrets of his own. Who doesn’t on this island?

She felt a sharp tug on her senses. §5“I feel them” §8rasped §5ɨȶ's§8 voice behind her. 
His presence was unsettling as always yet oddly comforting. She knew he would protect her.
#- §5“We must hurry my dear.” ɨȶ §8hovered behind her, a mass of shifting shadows and eyes shining that she could never quite follow. §5“The Lanterns call to me. And I’m hungry.”

§8With a whispered spell, Sweetpea summoned a small wooden boat, it's oars moving on their 
#- §8own to glide them across the unnaturally still water. She thought going by boat in the shadows would be less risky than walking over the bridge. The silence set her teeth on edge, but she tried to focus on the mission. §0Soul Lanterns§8; forged to capture the essence of magical beings.
#- §8Sweetpea believed these things had to be highly illegal, but she had no right to judge. Sweetpea needed them, or rather, §5ɨȶ§8 did.

Sweetpea hopped out, her boots barely making a sound. Sweetpea was good at stealth when she had to be. §5ɨȶ§8 slithered after her...
#- §8pressing against her back like a second shadow trying to make her pick up the pace. Sweetpea waved a hand dismissively. 
§6“We can’t just barge in. You know how this works, they don’t just trap souls, they trap magic. One wrong step, and we’ll end up like those poor beings already trapped."
#- §5“They deserved it.” ɨȶ’s §8voice was low and guttural, but there was a hint of fondness in the way he lingered around her. §5“You do not.” 

§8Sweetpea ignored 
the comment.

The factory’s interior was as not a surprise.
A cold empty space.
#- §8The air reeked of burnt magic, sharp and acidic. Conveyor belts groaned under the weight of enchanted potions being processed, their eerie glow casting 
the room in an otherworldly light.

Sweetpea shivered 
as the whispers began.
#- §8Faint, mournful cries emanating from the crack in the walls.

§5“There” ɨȶ §8hissed, 
one of his tendril-like fingers pointing toward a pile of lanterns at the far end of the room. Each pulsating faintly like a dying heartbeat. Sweetpea approached cautiously. 
#- §8She hesitated. Something about these lanterns felt… wrong. 

The air around them seemed heavier.

Charged with a more oppressive energy than normal. 

§6“These aren’t 
normal strength…” §8she muttered.
#- §5“Take them,” ɨȶ §8said, his voice soft but insistent. §5“You are strong enough.”

§8Sweetpea reached for the nearest lantern. The moment her fingers touched the cold metal, a searing pain shot up her arm! She cried out as the lantern’s glow flared, pulling at her magic...
#- §8Her eyes glowed blue and and she stared blankly. Her knees buckled, and her mind blurred, almost possessed as the lantern’s pull grew stronger, her power rapidly fading.

§5“Sweetpea!” 
ɨȶ’s §8voice was sharp now, aggressive and filled with urgency! 
#- §8But he was nothing but a glorified ghost and felt helpless. She tried to fight back, but her hand was stuck, the lantern’s power binding her in place. Her breath came in ragged gasps as her magic drained away, leaving her hollow. Her vibrant skin turning pale and withered.
#- §8Her petals drying out and turning brittle.

Suddenly, §5ɨȶ §8surged forward with all his might, his shadowy form engulfing her. 

He wrapped around her hand, prying it free with a force that was both tender 
and unnervingly possessive. 
#- §8Once Sweetpeas hand was free, §5ɨȶ§8 lunged for the lantern itself and consumed everything it had. 

The lantern snuffed out with a sickening hiss.

Sweetpea collapsed into §5ɨȶ’s§8 embrace... 

her body lifeless. 
#- §8He did not know how it was possible that he had summoned the energy and power to physically touch her, but he cradled her like a cocoon, holding her steady, fearing the worst.

Time passed. 

Sweetpea's silence 
was deafening.
#- §5“I will not lose you.              You are mine… 
I protect... 
            what is mine!”§r









   §6“Thanks… I think.”§r
#- §8Sweetpea had been awake for at least a minute without §5ɨȶ §8realising. §6“You are so creepy”§8. §5ɨȶ§8 dropped her on the ground instantly with a big thud. §5“That should be enough to keep me satisfied, for now,” ɨȶ §8grumbled. Sweetpea let out a weak laugh and got to her feet. 
A little wobbly, but 
#- §8slowly regaining her strength and magic. 

Her vibrant colour returning as she picked off the few rotten petals left.

§6“Let’s just grab a few and get out of here,” §8she said. 

Her voice shaky 
but determined. 
#- §8With §5ɨȶ’s§8 help, they managed to stuff a handful of lanterns into the boat without touching them directly. The whispers grew louder as they fled the factory. 

Back at the tavern, Sweetpea slumped into her chair, tossing 
the lanterns 
onto the table.
#- §8Sweetpea sighed, pouring herself a strong drink. 

§6“Next time, you’re doing the heavy lifting. I’m getting too old 
for this nonsense.”

§5ɨȶ§8 chuckled. 
§5“Well if you were immortal like me, none of that would have happened my dear”. 
#- §8Even after how close she’d come to losing everything, as the lanterns hummed softly on the table, Sweetpea couldn’t help but feel a strange sense of satisfaction. 

They had won, barely, but in their world, survival was 
victory enough.
